// REQUIRES: long
// P03.24 Done-when size for the operator checks, shape `overloads`: a generated
// program of size 400 checks without a crash, within a CPU-time ceiling of
// three times its cost alone, counted in units of `gopp version`
// (tests/cpu-limit.py; also in the ASan build). No
// ratio check: the generator makes about 5000
// uses for any N up to 5000, so N and 16 N are not the same work scaled, and
// past about 3000 overloads the check grows quadratically with their number
// (default build: 3200 0.13 s, 6400 0.49 s, 12800 1.98 s: task P03.27, which
// replaces the ceiling with a ratio check). One test per
// shape so lit runs the
// shapes in parallel. The parser allows 1024 levels of nesting, so a chain of
// operands is cut into expressions of 1000 operands (the same limit holds for
// an `int` sum).
// RUN: %python %S/Inputs/gen-ops-stress.py overloads 400 > %t.gopp
// RUN: %{cpu_limit} 14 24 -- %gopp check -check-j=1 --check-error-limit=0 %t.gopp
package main
